# PairBrowse secrets (dotenv format). Only your user account can read this file.
#
# Claude types a secret by writing its NAME (e.g. SHOPIFY_PASSWORD) as the value. PairBrowse
# swaps in the real value and masks it as <secret>NAME</secret> in everything Claude reads back,
# so Claude never sees it.
#
# Every secret needs a NAME_DOMAINS line: the sites it may be typed into (HTTPS only, subdomains
# included). A secret without one is never typed anywhere. This stops a malicious page from
# tricking Claude into typing your password into the page's own form.
#
# For accounts that matter most, prefer typing passwords yourself or using a password manager.
#
# SHOPIFY_PASSWORD=
# SHOPIFY_PASSWORD_DOMAINS=accounts.shopify.com
